  message: "Done in PR #2249 (dev 14e3b8b65). Evidence against the close condition:\n(1) THE TEST. tests/test_shared_fixture_contexts.py runs a throwaway project under pytest without xdist and with -n 2. test_folded_every_user_is_paired_with_the_code_the_fixture_ran: two tests share a module fixture and both are paired with the function only the fixture calls, with statement records {0, 1} each; a test that reaches a session fixture only through an already-built fixture is paired with its code too. 14 tests per mode.\n(2) A FULL RUN FOLDED on the branch (smart-test --full, 2026-11-18): 41,220 passed, 12 skipped, 30 xfailed in 698 s. The fold printed: shared work: 66 fixture context(s) with measured code; 41262 test(s) given their rows; 0 context(s) no test is recorded using. Unmeasured tests 8,770 (8,733 before).\n(3) LIVE CONTROL. Planted fault: entrypoints._take_dealing_ties, 'cut_score = ...' assigned None; ran tests/test_stable_id_floor_gate.py, whose module fixture 'runs' is the only route to that function for its tests. 24 passed, 7 errors. Before the fold the index paired 0 of the two measured failing tests with the function; after it, 7 tests of that file. Run record: failed_reaching_a_narrowed_block names the 2 measured failing tests; failed_not_selected is []. The other 5 failing tests are in unmeasured_test (their own call runs no measured code): the by-statement selector never narrows them away, and it does not count them. File: fast_smart_test_build_11172026/fixtures/live_control.txt.\n(4) MUTATIONS. 24 planted across the plugin, the fold and the reader; 23 went red. The survivor removes the plugin's 'coverage is started' check, which mirrors pytest-cov's own check and is not reached with coverage unstarted in any run I could build.\nNOT COVERED: a shared fixture fetched with request.getfixturevalue inside another shared fixture that was already built on that worker is not recorded as nested (0 such uses in the repository's tests outside the plugin's own tests). State an object keeps after its fixture returned it: WI-supar. Decorator caches: WI-masad.\nSIDE EFFECT TO KNOW: every test is now paired with analyze/registry.py lines 907-908 through the session autouse fixture that calls ensure_discovered, so file-level narrowing keeps every test for a change to that file.\n"  # 9552
